            "review_title": "Review at Captain Phook",
            "review_text": "Emmaandjim\nAuckland Central, New Zealand49 contributions\n0\nHooked on Captain Phook’s!\nSep 2022 • Friends\nWhat an awesome discovery. Our last night in HCMC and we tried Captain Phook’s. We were downstairs in the tiny dining area overlooking the kitchen and I have to say it was immaculate and the multiple chefs working together and around each other was ballet like! Also immaculately clean. The food was great. Between 3 we had salmon croquettes, salad leaves with eggplant & sun dried tomato and garlic prawns to start. That was followed by a spaghetti bolognese, a spaghetti with pistachio, pesto and prawns and the herbed lamb chops. We shared a torrija and ice cream to finish. All washed down with some Rooster blonde bia.\nRead more\nWritten September 11, 2022",
